learnings:
  - 'A convene/self-study finding can be a confident FALSE POSITIVE: Cid''s ''done children missing settledAt = invisible settlement debt'' rested on a misread of the field-ownership model — settledAt is stamped on the parent epic only (task-settlement.ts:365-375), so children correctly lack it and a child sweep would noise-flag every done task. Verifying findings before fixing is what caught it.'
  - The right place to lock a confusion-matrix's falsifiability is a unit test on the partition function itself (score()) fed synthetic per-cell inputs — far more controllable than constructing real git-conflict fixtures, and it targets exactly the mislabel regression (m&&g misfiled).
  - 'Accessibility token discipline: a deliberately-low-contrast token (--cut 2.6:1) is fine for strikethrough/bar-fills/redundant-color counters but must never color standalone readable text; promote those to --linen-400 (5.0+). A semantic anchor near the AA floor (--seam 4.52) needs a guard comment so future value changes re-run the contrast calc.'
